cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite this archive and the two papers listed under references."
title: "Code and data for: A Casimir turning point as the beginning of a small flat universe"
type: software
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23434067
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ailun-Zhang/casimir-cosmology"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - GPL-2.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Code, archived production results and figure scripts that reproduce the numbers and figures of two papers on a
  small flat universe (cubic three-torus) that begins at a Casimir turning point: the Standard-Model Casimir weight and
  the gauge/Higgs zero-mode energy, the shape Hessian and the emptiness gate, the quantum shape state at the turn and
  its nonlinear survival, the Higgs zero-mode criterion for the survival of the electroweak vacuum through the turn
  (critical top-quark masses, error budget, xi_H condition), and the CMB readability of the shape fossil. Every result
  directory has a quick and a full run mode and compares fresh output with the archived values under stated
  tolerances. Version 1.2.0 adds the Letter's Supplemental Material (static box and abelian Higgs model), the figures
  and derived numbers of the technical report version 1.1, an independent blind recalculation of the abelian Higgs
  check, and the report itself.
